 아침 7시에 일어납니다. 그리고 나서, 저는 [[☃ dropdown 1]].\n\n(I wake up at 7 AM in the morning. And then, I [[☃ dropdown 1]].)","images":{},"widgets":{"dropdown 1":{"type":"dropdown","options":{"placeholder":"select one","choices":[{"content":"아침을 먹습니다.","correct":true,"misconception":null},{"content":"잠을 잡니다.","correct":false,"misconception":"Confuses 'wake up' with 'sleep' or misunderstands the sequence of events."},{"content":"학교에 갑니다.","correct":false,"misconception":"Jumps to a later step in the morning routine, skipping an common intermediate action."},{"content":"숙제를 합니다.","correct":false,"misconception":"Places an activity (homework) in an atypical part of the morning routine."}],"static":false},"graded":true,"version":{"major":0,"minor":0},"alignment":"default","static":false}}},"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"The sentence describes what someone does first thing in the morning: \"I wake up at 7 AM.\" Think about what most people typically do right after waking up and before starting their day.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The Korean phrase \"일어납니다\" means \"wake up.\" After waking up, a common next step in a daily routine is to eat the first meal of the day. What is that meal called, and how would you say 'eat' in Korean?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The action of 'eating breakfast' in Korean is \"아침을 먹습니다.\" This fits logically after waking up and before going to school or doing other activities.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":null,"dash_metadata":{"dash_question_id":"ai_q_adafdf459bd4","skill_ids":["ai_gen_korean_us_6-8th-grade-korean-novice-mid-proficiency_unit_naui-haru-my-daily-routine"],"difficulty":0.5,"expected_time_seconds":60.0,"slug":"ai_q_adafdf459bd4","skill_names":["나의 하루 (My Daily Routine)"],"unit_id":"ai_gen_korean_us_6-8th-grade-korean-novice-mid-proficiency_unit_naui-haru-my-daily-routine","lesson_id":"ai_gen_korean_us_6-8th-grade-