xercise_name":"Practice","ai_generated":true,"source":"gemini"}},{"question":{"content":"[[☃ image 1]]\n\nYou are talking with a new friend about your favorite foods. You want to say, 'I like pizza the most!' Which of these Korean sentences correctly expresses this? [[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"저는 피자를 가장 좋아해요.","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false,"misconception":null},{"content":"저는 피자가 맛있어요.","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false,"misconception":"Confuses 'I like' with 'It is delicious' or 'Pizza is tasty'."},{"content":"저는 피자이 가장 좋아해요.","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false,"misconception":"Uses the subject particle '이' instead of the object particle '을/를' after the food."},{"content":"저는 피자를 좋아해요.","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false,"misconception":"Omits 'the most,' making the preference less specific than 'I like pizza the most!'"}],"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true,"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"numCorrect":1},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":2,"minor":0}},"image 1":{"type":"image","graded":false,"version":{"major":0,"minor":0},"alignment":"block","static":false,"options":{"backgroundImage":{"url":"http://localhost:8000/static/images/c40a8a89ffd628b7.png","width":400,"height":300},"alt":"Illustration for 좋아하는 음식 (Favorite Foods)","caption":""}}}},"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"To say 'I like X' in Korean, you need the subject '저는' (I), the object 'X' (e.g., pizza), and the verb '좋아해요' (like). What particle do you need to attach to the object 'pizza'?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"When you like an object in Korean, you attach the object particle -을/를 to the noun (e.g., 피자**를**). To emphasize 'the most' or 'favorite,' you often add the word 가장 before the verb '좋아해요'.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{